Overview

The Geospatial Multi‑Physics Stratum Simulator (GMSS) is a unified planetary‑scale simulation engine integrating astrophysical forcing, geomechanics, multiphase subsurface flow, fracture mechanics, biogeochemical ecosystems, and cryptographic verification.

GMSS models Earth’s subsurface as a coupled, evolving, multi‑domain system, where physics, biology, chemistry, and cosmic forcing interact through a single governed state vector. All simulation steps are validated using zero‑knowledge proofs and stored in an immutable ledger.

GMSS is designed for researchers in geophysics, Earth system science, computational physics, cryptography, and planetary modeling.

